    "notes": "1. 'Total revenues and other income' is mapped to 'total_revenue' and is the sum of its three listed components. 2. 'Total costs and other deductions' is not used directly. Instead, 'total_operating_cost' is constructed from all cost line items that are considered operational in the oil & gas industry, excluding 'Interest expense' and 'Other taxes and duties'. 'Other taxes and duties' (e.g., production, property, excise taxes) are considered part of the cost of revenue for this industry and are included within 'Production and manufacturing expenses' and 'Selling, general and administrative expenses' per Note 19, so they are not listed separately to avoid double-counting. 3. 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' is mapped to 'net_income'. 4. 'Income tax expense (benefit)' is mapped to 'taxes'. 5. 'Interest expense' is mapped to 'interest_expenses'. 6. All values are taken directly from the primary income statement table. Supplementary tables provide detail but do not change the top-line figures used. 7. The sign convention for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost follows rule 13: these are income-reducing items, so the positive numbers from the statement are reported as positive.",
